    ":question/math-academy-id": "q-132255",
    ":question/problem": "For the function $g(x,y,z)=\\sqrt{x}\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(y{z}^{2}),$ evaluate $\\frac{∂g}{∂z}$ at the point $(3,\\frac{1}{2},1).$",
    ":question/worked-solution": "We differentiate the given function with respect to $z,$ treating all other variables as constants. \n\nUsing the constant multiple and chain rules, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂g}{∂z} & =\\frac{∂}{∂z}(\\sqrt{x}\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(y{z}^{2})) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{x}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂z}(\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(y{z}^{2})) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{x}\\cdot \\left(-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{(y{z}^{2})}^{2}}}\\right)\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂z}(y{z}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{x}\\cdot \\left(-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{y}^{2}{z}^{4}}}\\right)\\cdot y\\cdot 2z \\\\  & =-\\frac{2yz\\sqrt{x}}{\\sqrt{1-{y}^{2}{z}^{4}}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the partial derivative at the point $(3,\\frac{1}{2},1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂g}{∂z}{|}_{(3,\\,1/2,\\,1)} & =-\\frac{2\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)(1)\\sqrt{3}}{\\sqrt{1-{\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)}^{2}(1)^{4}}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{\\sqrt{1-\\frac{1}{4}}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\right)} \\\\  & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$"
  },
