    ":question/math-academy-id": "q-35715",
    ":question/problem": "Find ${g}_{y}(x,y,z)$ given that $g(x,y,z)=z\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(xy).$",
    ":question/worked-solution": "We differentiate the given function with respect to $y,$ treating all other variables as constants. \n\nUsing the constant multiple and chain rules, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}_{y}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(z\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(xy)) \\\\  & =z\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(xy)) \\\\  & =z\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-(xy)^{2}}}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}(xy) \\\\  & =z\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-(xy)^{2}}}\\cdot (x) \\\\  & =\\frac{xz}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}{y}^{2}}}\\end{aligned}\n$$"
  },
