    ":question/math-academy-id": "q-132251",
    ":question/problem": "Find ${f}_{x}(x,y,z)$ for $f(x,y,z)={cos}^{2}⁡(3x-{y}^{2}).$",
    ":question/worked-solution": "We differentiate the given function with respect to $x,$ treating all other variables as constants. \n\nUsing the chain rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({cos}^{2}⁡(3x-{y}^{2})) \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x-{y}^{2})\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x-{y}^{2})) \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x-{y}^{2})\\cdot (-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x-{y}^{2}))\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(3x-{y}^{2}) \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x-{y}^{2})\\cdot (-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x-{y}^{2}))\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =-6\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x-{y}^{2})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x-{y}^{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$"
  },
