    ":question/id": "c701d949-2d48-5058-b224-6149f2ad0e9c",
    ":question/problem": "Find $\\dfrac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}$ for $f(x,y,z)=xy^2+z^3.$ Treat $x$ and $z$ as constants.",
    ":question/worked-solution": "Hold $x$ and $z$ fixed. The factor $x$ is a constant multiplier, and $z^3$ is independent of $y$.\n\nUsing the sum, constant multiple, and power rules,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}&=x\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial y}(y^2)+\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial y}(z^3)\\\\\n&=x(2y)+0\\\\\n&=2xy.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"
  },
