    ":question/id": "4f001fc3-1ece-55d3-b468-098ed948154d",
    ":question/problem": "Find $g_y(x,y,z)$ for $g(x,y,z)=(x+z)\\sin y+(y+z)\\cos x.$",
    ":question/worked-solution": "Differentiate with respect to $y$, holding $x$ and $z$ fixed. Thus $x+z$ and $\\cos x$ are constants, while $y+z$ has derivative $1$.\n\nUsing the sum and constant multiple rules,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ng_y(x,y,z)&=(x+z)\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial y}(\\sin y)+\\cos x\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial y}(y+z)\\\\\n&=(x+z)\\cos y+\\cos x(1+0)\\\\\n&=(x+z)\\cos y+\\cos x.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"
  },
